{
  "id": "T-1416",
  "created_at": 1790806127.912265,
  "parent": "T-1403",
  "role": "review",
  "tier": "sonnet",
  "complexity": 7,
  "title": "review: New orchestrator/machine.py: machine-wide leases and account usage ledger shared by every repo",
  "spec": "Why: goal T-1403 W4. Accounts, Claude worker slots and gate resources (simulators, ports) are machine-wide, but each repo keeps its own STATE/pool_state.json (pool.py:13, 471-473), so three repos each believe they own the full Claude cap. This task only adds the module; wiring is later tasks (C1, C2, C4, C6).\nContract (exact):\n- MACHINE_DIR = Path(os.environ.get(\"ORCH_MACHINE_DIR\", \"~/.orchestrator-machine\")).expanduser(); files leases.json, accounts.json; all reads and writes under an fcntl flock on MACHINE_DIR/machine.lock; writes atomic (tmp + os.replace).\n- acquire(kind: str, cap: int, holder: dict) -> str | None; holder = {\"repo\": str, \"task\": str, \"pid\": int}; sweeps dead pids of that kind first; returns a lease id (uuid4 hex) or None at cap.\n- release(lease_id: str) -> None (idempotent).\n- count(kind: str) -> int (sweeps dead pids first).\n- record_usage(account_id: str, tokens: int, *, repo: str, planner: bool = False, now: float | None = None) -> None.\n- usage(account_id: str, now: float | None = None) -> {\"window_tokens\": int, \"day_tokens\": int, \"planner_window_tokens\": int, \"planner_day_tokens\": int}; window 5 h rolling from the first record in the window, day = local calendar day (Europe/Zurich via time.localtime).\n- Lease kinds used later: \"claude_worker\", \"gate:<resource>\".\nPure module: import only stdlib. Tests set ORCH_MACHINE_DIR to a temp dir.\n\nWork on the task branch cut from goal/T-1403. Commit first, then run the focused acceptance test in the foreground (uv run python -m pytest <id> -q). Never background a command and never run the full gate; the daemon gates externally. Acceptance ids are tests/<file>.py::<function or method name>; write the test as a unittest.TestCase method using tests/_harness.py like the neighbouring tests.",
  "inputs": [
    "T-1408"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_machine.py::test_worker_slot_cap_spans_repos passes: two holders from different repo paths acquire claude_worker leases up to cap, the next acquire returns None, releasing one frees a slot, and a lease whose pid is dead is swept by count()",
    "tests/test_machine.py::test_usage_ledger_sums_across_repos passes: record_usage from two repos for one account sums in usage(account) window and day totals, with rollover at the 5-hour window and the local day",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh wt/THIS-TASK exits 0"
  ],
  "scope": [
    "orchestrator/machine.py",
    "tests/test_machine.py"
  ],
  "depends_on": [],
  "constraints": {
    "read_only": true,
    "budget_turns": 20,
    "timeout_s": 900
  },
  "status": "done",
  "assigned_to": "claude:A",
  "worktree": "/Users/k3ntaw/code/orchestrator/wt/T-1416",
  "codex_thread": null,
  "result": {
    "summary": "Verified against contract: MACHINE_DIR/leases.json/accounts.json/machine.lock, flock-guarded reads/writes, atomic tmp+os.replace writes, acquire/release/count/record_usage/usage signatures and semantics all match. Pure stdlib import. Ran both acceptance tests (test_worker_slot_cap_spans_repos, test_usage_ledger_sums_across_repos) via unittest discover \u2014 both pass. Checked window/day rollover arithmetic and pid-liveness sweep logic; no correctness issues found. One low-severity dead-code nit in usage()'s write-guard condition, not worth blocking on.",
    "verdict": "approve",
    "comments": [
      {
        "path": "orchestrator/machine.py",
        "line": 163,
        "issue": "In usage(), the condition `account_id not in accounts` is always False because accounts.setdefault(account_id, ...) just added it two lines above, so a freshly-created account is never persisted via that branch. Not a functional bug (an unpersisted fresh account still round-trips to zeroed defaults next call), but the check is dead/misleading and should probably just be `changed`.",
        "severity": "low"
      }
    ],
    "packet_version": "e8dd266666c8",
    "confidence": 0.0,
