    {
      "ts": 1790806262.406085,
      "status": "done",
      "result": {
        "summary": "Verified against contract: MACHINE_DIR/leases.json/accounts.json/machine.lock, flock-guarded reads/writes, atomic tmp+os.replace writes, acquire/release/count/record_usage/usage signatures and semantics all match. Pure stdlib import. Ran both acceptance tests (test_worker_slot_cap_spans_repos, test_usage_ledger_sums_across_repos) via unittest discover \u2014 both pass. Checked window/day rollover arithmetic and pid-liveness sweep logic; no correctness issues found. One low-severity dead-code nit in usage()'s write-guard condition, not worth blocking on.",
        "verdict": "approve",
        "comments": [
          {
            "path": "orchestrator/machine.py",
            "line": 163,
            "issue": "In usage(), the condition `account_id not in accounts` is always False because accounts.setdefault(account_id, ...) just added it two lines above, so a freshly-created account is never persisted via that branch. Not a functional bug (an unpersisted fresh account still round-trips to zeroed defaults next call), but the check is dead/misleading and should probably just be `changed`.",
            "severity": "low"
          }
        ],
        "packet_version": "e8dd266666c8",
